+Restyle this terrain image for efficient bitmap-to-vector tracing. KEEP EXACT OVERALL COMPOSITION, terrace arrangement, all route connections, stairways, bridges, arch openings, and architectural silhouettes. Transparent background. Make a substantially simpler FLAT SCREEN-PRINT VECTOR ILLUSTRATION, not a painting or 3D render.
+CRITICAL: every broad surface is ONE perfectly uniform opaque color. At most 10-12 flat colors in the entire image. NO gradients, NO ambient occlusion, NO glow, NO texture, NO flecks/noise, NO bevel highlights, NO woodgrain. Each rock mass only 2 or 3 large clean polygonal shadow planes. Large outer edges retain organic distinctive shape. Irregular silhouette stays.
+Replace tiny repeated details with well-designed larger shapes: roof tiles represented by 4-6 broad dark bands only, masonry walls by a few large irregular joined stone blocks, foliage by clustered silhouettes with minimal internal veins. No little highlight dots on every roof tile. No mesh/net patterns; plain hanging cloth silhouette instead. No tiny chips or individual grass blades. Important structural braces, rail connections, and steps remain visible and continuous.
+Professional side-view game environment illustration. Preserve cold blue/slate rock, muted green tops, restrained warm brown timber. Avoid oversaturated yellow-green and avoid overly round/blobby posterization. Readable hard-edged shapes. Do not add new objects. No background colors outside the terrain. Entire assembly in frame, no cropping. The goal is natural rich macroforms built from FEW LARGE FLAT SHAPES, not thousands of tiny shapes.
